FUN_0000_1d59 (mouse-cursor sprite-tree walker): restore the DS=word[DGROUP:0x3e02] list base.

Called by FUN_0000_1cdb / FUN_0000_1c6a during INT-33h mouse-cursor init.  1cdb does `mov ds,[DGROUP:\n0x3e02]` (=0x1faf, the cursor/sprite-list segment) right before the call (asm 0x1d40); Ghidra dropped it,
so `[bx]`/`[bx+2]` lost their DS base and were dereferenced as host pointers (SIGSEGV).  The `[bp+di]`
byte marks are SS(=DGROUP)-based, the walk stride is 0xc bytes, and the fields are 16-bit words -- Ghidras
int* arithmetic mis-scaled both.  Reconstruct faithfully; ax(=limit=param_1) is preserved -> the return.
